> north
Hall

The hall is long and glass-framed, with a caretaker standing where the shadows gather.

You can see a caretaker.

Available exits: east, south, west.

The floorboards answer your first step with a tired creak.

> west
Kitchen

The kitchen is narrow and white-tiled. Its cupboards are too orderly for a room that should have fed people.

You can see a kitchen cabinet.

Available exits: east.
!room kitchen

> open cabinet
You open the kitchen cabinet. The hinges move without complaint.

> look in cabinet
In the kitchen cabinet is a pair of garden shears.
!contains garden shears

> take shears from cabinet
You take the pair of garden shears.

> east
Hall

The hall is long and glass-framed, with a caretaker standing where the shadows gather.

You can see a caretaker.

Available exits: east, south, west.

> east
Conservatory

Glass ribs hold the rain above ranks of empty planters. The room smells of damp earth kept too long indoors.

Available exits: west.

The conservatory air is warmer than the hall and much less alive.
!room conservatory

> use shears
You trim the dead stems away from the glass. Behind them, a cracked pane catches the rain.
!flag garden_cut_back
!contains cracked pane

> read pane
The crack is not lettering, but your eye keeps making a word from it: safe.
!flag safe_means_trapped

> use shears on pane
You work the shears into the crack, but the glass has already shown you all it can.
